Replace strncpy() with strscpy() for Linux 7.2 compatibility.

Linux 7.2 removed strncpy() from the kernel-space string API (see the Phoronix
"Linux 7.2 Drops strncpy" coverage; 360+ upstream commits). NVIDIA 580.173.02 —
the last driver branch supporting Maxwell/Pascal/Volta — still calls strncpy()
in five places in its OS-glue layer, so its kernel modules fail to compile on
7.2 with an implicit-declaration error.

strscpy() is the kernel's drop-in replacement for the bounded-copy-with-
NUL-termination use case and has existed since Linux 4.3, so the patched driver
still builds on every older kernel this repository ships. The two wrapper
functions that returned strncpy()'s value (the destination pointer) are rewritten
to return dest explicitly, since strscpy() returns a length, not a pointer.

Call sites and context verified against the NVIDIA-Linux-x86_64-580.173.02 source
tree. Mirrors the community fix (babiulep/my-kernel-patches, CachyOS
kernel-patches 7.2/misc/nvidia). Applied to the shared driver source, so it
covers both the closed ("legacy_580") and open module builds.

--- a/kernel/nvidia/os-interface.c
+++ b/kernel/nvidia/os-interface.c
@@ -759,7 +759,7 @@ void NV_API_CALL os_get_current_process_name(char *buf, NvU32 len)
 void NV_API_CALL os_get_current_process_name(char *buf, NvU32 len)
 {
     task_lock(current);
-    strncpy(buf, current->comm, len - 1);
+    strscpy(buf, current->comm, len - 1);
     buf[len - 1] = '\0';
     task_unlock(current);
 }
--- a/kernel/nvidia/linux_nvswitch.c
+++ b/kernel/nvidia/linux_nvswitch.c
@@ -2058,7 +2058,7 @@
         return -NVL_ERR_GENERIC;
     }

-    strncpy(regkey_val, regkey_val_start, regkey_val_len);
+    strscpy(regkey_val, regkey_val_start, regkey_val_len);
     regkey_val[regkey_val_len] = '\0';

     if (nvswitch_os_strtouint(regkey_val, data) != 0)
@@ -2413,7 +2413,8 @@ nvswitch_os_strncpy
     NvLength length
 )
 {
-    return strncpy(dest, src, length);
+    strscpy(dest, src, length);
+    return dest;
 }

